<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lausanne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lausanne is a city on the northern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-geneva">Lake Geneva</a>, the capital of the Swiss canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaud">Vaud</a>. It was the seat of a bishopric from about 600, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> ruled the town as princes until Bern conquered Vaud in 1536 and introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>. Its Gothic cathedral was consecrated in 1275, and the city is now home to the Federal Supreme Court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> and the International Olympic Committee.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lausanne.jpg" alt="Lausanne" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arnaud Gaillard (arnaud amarys.com); Gzzz; Roland Zumbühl. Original uploader was Hagelhans at de.wikipedia; Rama; Composition: Noldo18 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lausanne_Wiki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
